          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. A snail is trying to climb along the wall of a deep well. During the day it climbs up ‘u’ cm and during the night it slowly slips down ‘d’ cm. This happens for 10 days and 10 nights.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.159,
            0.859,
            0.198
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) Write an expression describing how far away the snail is from its starting position.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.212,
            0.736,
            0.25
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) What can we say about the snail’s movement if d > u? Ans:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.265,
            0.309,
            0.283
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) 10 (u − d) cm"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.299,
            0.655,
            0.341
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) If d > u, the snail slips down more than it climbs. This means the snail will never reach the top."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.358,
            0.884,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Radha is preparing for a cycling race and practices daily. The first week she cycles 5 km every day. Every week she increases the daily distance cycled by ‘z’ km. How many kilometers would Radha have cycled after 3 weeks?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.462,
            0.299,
            0.48
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 105 + 21z km"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
